    # affiliation: '[Your institution]'
abstract: >-
  Artifact evaluating OpenMP target offloading against each vendor's native
  programming model (CUDA, HIP and SYCL) for intra-node multi-GPU programming
  on NVIDIA H100, AMD MI250X and Intel Data Center GPU Max 1550 GPUs.

  A 3D variable-coefficient heat-equation solver is decomposed across the GPUs
  inside a single node under four halo-exchange strategies (blocking, task-based
  with nowait, one host thread per device, and direct device-to-device copies),
  at 2 and 4 GPUs. A single unmodified set of OpenMP sources is compiled on all
  three vendors. The artifact also contains a hidden-helper-thread sensitivity
  study, intra-node bandwidth and latency microbenchmarks that supply the
  constants for an analytical performance model, and the complete raw
  measurement data, so every figure in the paper can be regenerated without GPU
  access.
